# Skill: stack-detector (PATTERN §19.2, v2.12)

> Adapter Cursor della skill `stack-detector` definita in `.claude/skills/stack-detector.md`.
> Costrutto: Cursor rule `.mdc`. File equivalente Claude Code: `.claude/skills/stack-detector.md`.

Riconosce lingua, framework, versione di un albero di codice.
Invocata da `code-review-protocol` Fase 1 e da `repo-extraction-protocol` Fase 2.

## Output schema

```json
{
  "language": "python | typescript | javascript | go | java | kotlin | rust | ruby | php | csharp | other",
  "framework": "fastapi | django | flask | express | nestjs | nextjs | react | vue | svelte | spring | gin | echo | actix | rails | laravel | dotnet | other | none",
  "framework_version": "string | unknown",
  "secondary_libs": ["<name>@<version>"],
  "patterns_expected": ["async | pydantic_v2 | hooks | ..."],
  "ruleset_id": "<language>.<framework>.v<major>",
  "confidence": 0.94,
  "evidence": [
    {"type": "manifest", "file": "pyproject.toml", "weight": 0.5}
  ]
}
```

Soglie `confidence`: `≥0.9` high (manifest+import+config coerenti); `0.6-0.9` medium; `<0.3` very low → segnala in chat.

## Algoritmo (3 fasi)

### Fase 1 — Manifest scan (peso 0.5)

| Manifest | Lingua | Framework |
|---|---|---|
| `package.json` | typescript (+ `tsconfig.json`) / javascript | react, vue, next, ... da `dependencies` |
| `pyproject.toml` | python | fastapi, django, flask da dipendenze |
| `requirements.txt` | python (fallback) | regex sui pacchetti |
| `go.mod` | go | gin, echo, fiber |
| `Cargo.toml` | rust | actix, axum |
| `pom.xml` | java | spring-boot |
| `build.gradle{.kts}` | java/kotlin | spring |
| `Gemfile` | ruby | rails |
| `composer.json` | php | laravel, symfony |
| `*.csproj` | csharp | dotnet |

### Fase 2 — Config framework (peso 0.2)

File di config noti: `next.config.{js,mjs}`, `vite.config.{js,ts}`, `nest-cli.json`, `manage.py`, `nuxt.config.{js,ts}`, `angular.json`, `tsconfig.json`, `Dockerfile` (regex su `FROM`).

### Fase 3 — Sampling import (peso 0.3)

Glob `**/*.<ext>`, campiona ≤50 file (priorità `src/`, `app/`, `cmd/`, `lib/`; salta `node_modules/`, `vendor/`, `.git/`, `dist/`). Regex sui primi 50 righe per import statements. Se ≥5 file importano il framework candidato → aggiungi weight 0.3. Divergenza → riduci confidence 0.2 + `evidence.type: "import-divergence"`.

`patterns_expected` derivati da `(language, framework, version)`:
- `python, fastapi ≥0.95` → `["async", "pydantic_v2", "dependency_injection"]`
- `typescript, react ≥18` → `["hooks", "concurrent_mode_compatible", "strict_mode"]`
- `go, gin` → `["middleware_chain", "context_propagation", "explicit_error_return"]`

## Casi limite

- **Monorepo multi-language**: produce `stack_descriptor[]` (array).
- **Manifest assente**: salta Fase 1; Fase 3 con peso aumentato (0.5); `confidence` cap 0.5.
- **Versione unknown**: `framework_version: "unknown"`, `confidence` cap 0.7, usa ruleset versione più recente.
- **Nessun framework**: `framework: "none"`, `ruleset_id: "<language>.none.v1"`.

## SSR Detection (opt-in `fe_correctness.ssr_aware.enabled: true`)

Emette `ssr_context` aggiuntivo:
```json
{
  "framework": "nextjs-app-router | nextjs-pages-router | nuxt3 | remix | sveltekit | none | unknown-ssr",
  "rendering_mode": "ssr | csr",
  "router_type": "app | pages | null",
  "revalidation_support": true
}
```

Priority rules: Next.js App Router (cartella `app/` + `page.tsx`) > Pages Router (`pages/_app.tsx`) > Nuxt3 > Remix > SvelteKit > none.

## Limitazioni Cursor

- **Glob**: usa `@<code_path>/` mention per caricare i manifest rilevanti.
- **Sampling**: leggi i file con `@<file>` mention; campiona max 50 file.
- **Stateless**: ogni invocazione ricalcola da zero. No cache.
